  "preamble": "Deaffrication of the voiceless lateral affricate [tɬ] to the voiceless lateral fricative [ɬ] drops the stop closure but keeps the lateral friction. In the Totonacan family, Proto-Totonac-Tepehua *ƛ [tɬ] became ɬ in all three Tepehua languages and in some Totonac languages (Misantla, Upper Necaxa), while Papantla, Apapantilla, Filomeno Mata and the Highland Totonac varieties kept the affricate.",
